assistant: Subject: read unit_amount when price is missing

In vendor-api-version 2026-10-01 the product field `price` was renamed to `unit_amount`, and the published spec doesn't mention it. `get_product` only read `p.price ?? null`, so for new-version responses it quietly returned `price: null`. The unit didn't change: both recordings of p-1001 show 1199 US dollars, which also fits the contract's 20–2000 USD range. The handler now reads `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`, and `unit_amount` is added to `VendorProduct` (in `src/tools/get_product.ts`). The old 2026-01-01 responses still use `price` and give exactly the same output as before. Typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test. One thing I haven't checked: `search_products` also reads only `p.price` from `/products`, so it may have the same problem if the new version renamed the field in search results too.

